  "notes": [
    "Strict configuration produced zero signals; semistrict and relaxed runs executed for calibration only.",
    "Added --start-offset to target newer closed-event windows and tested strict strategy across offset ranges.",
    "Observed strict signals remain zero across tested windows; failures are dominated by no_history or strict lifecycle/edge constraints.",
    "Read local prediction-market and behavioral papers; tested reverse favorite-longshot (YES-side) hypothesis explicitly.",
    "Added offset-aware and side-aware tests; semistrict NO/best on offset 3000 currently dominates with small sample (+0.55% over 3 fills).",
    "Blocker fix: alpha_sweep_ssrn now prints offset-level coverage diagnostics and supports min_fills gating.",
    "Identified actionable window: offset 3000 has 100% history coverage on strict candidates but strict timing/edge removes most trades.",
    "Added throughput metrics (avg/peak fills per 3-day window) to backtest output.",
    "Lax 3-day profile achieved peak 200 fills in a 3-day window with real entries/exits; profitability remained marginal/negative in sampled run.",
    "Current task adds a live research/reporting interface rather than another thesis-specific backtest variant.",
    "The new agent interface is intended to make market probability, estimated probability, EV, sizing, and portfolio risk explicit in one output.",
    "autonomous_agent.py now scans live active markets, estimates probabilities with a debiased favorite-longshot model, sizes positions with capped fractional Kelly, and writes local report snapshots.",
    "test_autonomous_agent.py covers EV, Kelly sizing, lifecycle bias behavior, and portfolio selection constraints.",
    "Current task adds an explicit paper-thesis model and a dedicated real-data backtest wrapper so the paper-inspired logic is separable from generic heuristics.",
    "paper_alpha.py now encodes the thesis directly: early window only, No side only, 70-99c No band, category-specific early bias uplift, fixed-size diversified deployment assumptions.",
    "paper_alpha_real_backtest.py verified the exact paper-mapped rules on a newer resolved window with real entry prices; sample run at offset 5000 generated 8 fills with 87.5% win rate but -0.03% ROI after paid prices.",
    "New task focuses on the observed live edge rather than the original early-lifecycle paper thesis: late-expiry No-side entries in sports spreads/totals plus emotional politics/headline binaries.",
    "Next task: add an acceleration preset and runtime caps that can approach a 100-position paper book without using oversized per-trade stakes.",
    "Acceleration preset now widens category caps, relaxes dedupe, and shrinks late-book sizing to push the live paper portfolio toward a 100-slot target.",
    "cycle_runner exports now include trade_count/open_trade_count/closed_trade_count aliases so downstream trackers can read the latest book summary directly.",
    "Validation on 2026-04-08: acceleration preset found 112 candidates and locked 79 paper positions from a $1,000 wallet with $461 deployed.",
    "Operational rebalance on 2026-04-08: scaled the 79 open acceleration positions pro-rata so the paper wallet is now 100% deployed.",
    "New task: replace mixed-sleeve acceleration with a paper-reset sports-derivatives-only preset and relaunch the paper wallet from $1,000.",
    "Added a paper_reset preset that bans politics, emotional headlines, moneylines, draws, and synthetic fills; it only trades sports spreads/totals.",
    "Reset the paper wallet from $1,000 and relaunched with paper_reset; current clean book holds 21 open sports derivative positions with $435 deployed."
  ]
}
